  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "After the explicit2-to-1 assumption and named invariance/Gaussian stability/PCP decoding background, the proof must construct the disjoint-coordinate noise operator with controlled spectrum, establish the new low-influence coloring stability lower bound and use paired-coordinate projections in a colorability-preserving verifier. Complete authored domain/influence bridge and verifier completeness/soundness are supplied. This new spectral/long-code reduction is one H2 conditional approximation-hardness task beyond routine application of a quoted PCP theorem.",
  "source_scope_note": "Exact original Theorem3.26 only: for every fixed k>=3, assuming the stated2-to-1 Conjecture, Max k-Colorable Subgraph has the original1-1/k+O(log k/k^2) approximation hardness. Entire conditional Section3 is retained, including label-cover assumption, disjoint-coordinate zero-diagonal noise operator and spectrum, influence/domain conventions, full new stability proposition, PCP verifier, completeness, soundness and decoding. The source-stated Majority-is-Stablest, KKMO Gaussian/decoding and CST weighted-to-unweighted inputs remain named prerequisites; no unconditional gadget result or appendix tripartite-PCP variant is selected or counted. All-page source/output QA completed; exact final actual logs have zero missing-glyph/reference/citation/stability/box or other warning lines. Source-material candidate only, no admission/remote-delivery credit.",
  "source_quirks_note": "The exact original2-to-1 conjecture paragraph retains its R_U=d R_V wording at native1013, and subsequent verifier retains the original (U,V,E,R,2R,Pi) convention. Original variables and all spectral/truncation/stability indices and display punctuation are preserved in full context; no relabeling, formula repair or mathematical-refereeing conclusion.",
